.pio
.clinerules
CLAUDE.md
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.VSCodeCounter/
.gitignore
.cache/
.claude/

# Real secrets - never commit. Use secrets.example.h as the shared template.
include/secrets.h
secrets.h

# WebUI build artifacts — generated by build_webui.py at compile time :3
webui/node_modules/
webui/dist/
webui/.env.local

# LittleFS data artifacts — generated by build pipeline, not hand-edited
data/index.html
data/index.html.gz

# Dev tools & diagnostic scripts — not part of the firmware.
# (tools/* not tools/ so specific files CAN be re-included below —
#  git cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory.)
tools/*
# SlopSync registry codegen IS part of the repo: spec<->code lockstep tool.
!tools/gen_registry_header.py
# SlopCanon mechanical floor (docs/canon/CANON.md §5) — doctrine enforcement
# is part of the repo for the same lockstep reason as the registry codegen.
!tools/canon_lint.py
# CHANNEL-MAP.md table codegen — same lockstep reason as the registry codegen:
# it parses registry.yaml (core) + SlopSyncCatalog.h (device) so the doc can
# never silently drift from the wire again after the RFC-047 renumber.
!tools/gen_channel_map.py
# Channel-space grid VISUAL generator (RFC-047 companion; output is generated
# per-run evidence, gitignored below like SlopScope captures).
!tools/gen_channel_grid.py
# Primary verification tool — operator ruling 2026-07-27: tracked (slopsoak
# imports its wire layer; an untracked verifier is one checkout from gone).
!tools/slopsync_probe.py
# Docs-site table codegen launcher. Same lockstep reason: the real generator
# lives in docs-site/tools/ so the site subtree stays extractable; this is the
# repo-root sibling that keeps the tools/ convention working.
!tools/gen_docs_tables.py
# SlopScope — the motion-pipeline oscilloscope (asked vs planned vs achieved).
# Tracked because it is an ECOSYSTEM-NAMED deliverable, not a scratch script:
# it ships with the protocol, is referenced from the docs site's testing guide,
# and is the tool an integrator reaches for when motion "feels wrong". A
# zero-collision name nobody can find in the repo would defeat the point.
# NOTE for the operator: tools/slopsync_probe.py is STILL ignored by the rule
# above. That is the project's long-standing choice, so it was left alone --
# but it is now this project's primary verification tool and it was heavily
# extended during the v1.0 base pass (readiness gate, blob transfer, pairing
# cycles, estop, bench-home, annotation audit). Worth deciding deliberately
# whether it should be tracked too; an untracked verifier is one clean
# checkout away from gone.
!tools/slopscope.py
# SlopSoak — the SlopSync stability/soak harness. Tracked because it is the
# EVIDENCE-GENERATING TOOL for the WebSocket transport migration
# (links2004/arduinoWebSockets -> ESP32Async AsyncWebSocket), not a scratch
# script: the before/after JSON summaries it emits are the whole argument that
# the new transport is actually better rather than merely newer, and
# docs/ws-transport-baseline.md is written against its output. A harness that
# lives only on one machine cannot be re-run to reproduce or refute a claim.
# NOTE: it IMPORTS tools/slopsync_probe.py for the wire layer (frame header,
# CBOR profile, builders, registry constants) rather than duplicating it — so
# the "should the probe be tracked?" question above is now load-bearing for
# this file too.
!tools/slopsoak.py
.clangd
.clang-format
.cache/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Working docs, audits, plans & UI mockups — scratch, not firmware
SD32-*.md
sd32-preview-*.html
waypoint_kinematics_audit.md
graph_screenshot_temp.html
compile_commands.json
NewPCB.md
HANDOFF.md
plan.md
PLAN_NewPCB_Migration.md
PLAN_OSSM_Parity.md

# Reference hardware docs / binaries — not source
PCB Layout.diy
AIM_servo_modbus_reference.md
AIM_Servo_Motor_Datasheet_EN_with_images.pdf

# Build outputs, captures & scratch artifacts — generated, not source.
# Root-anchored + explicit per-tree rules: a bare `build/` here silently
# swallowed docs-site/docs/build/ (authored pages, never build output).
/build/
sim/slopsim/build/
sim/slopbench/build/
test/fuzz/build/
$null
flashpack/

# .NET build output (clients/)
clients/**/bin/
clients/**/obj/

# SlopSync fuzz gate (test/fuzz) — build outputs and scratch corpora.
# test/fuzz/build/ is ignored explicitly above. Only test/fuzz/corpus/ (the
# committed seed set) and the sources belong in git; see test/fuzz/README.md.
test/fuzz/work/
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*

# SlopScope diagnostic captures (tools/slopscope.py) — traces and rendered
# graphs are per-session evidence, not source. Share the .html file directly.
slopscope-*.jsonl
slopscope-*.html

# Generated channel-grid visual (tools/gen_channel_grid.py)
docs/slopsync/channel-grid.html

# SlopSoak run summaries (tools/slopsoak.py) — same reasoning as SlopScope's
# captures: per-run evidence, regenerated by re-running the harness. The
# baseline numbers that matter are quoted in docs/ws-transport-baseline.md.
slopsoak-*.json
